    "intro": "We have all taken that perfect selfie, only to look at it later and realize the camera flipped it backward so any text on your shirt is completely unreadable. Or maybe you downloaded an image from your phone to your computer, and suddenly it is sitting sideways. It is a tiny annoyance, but it totally ruins a good picture. Trying to fix it shouldn't require you to fire up a complicated, heavy photo editing program just to turn the thing ninety degrees. You just want it facing the right way so you can post it or send it. Fortunately, you can fix these orientation issues in seconds using free, web-based tools. You don't need any technical skills, and you certainly don't need to pay for software. Let's look at the easiest way to correct your photos so they look exactly the way you intended.",
