        "h2": "Straightening crooked photos",
        "text": "Sometimes, your photo isn't completely sideways. Maybe you just held the camera slightly tilted, and the horizon line looks like it is sliding downhill. A simple ninety-degree rotate won't fix this. What you need is fine-tuned rotation or a straighten tool. Many online editors have a slider that lets you rotate the image just one or two degrees at a time. This is perfect for fixing crooked horizons in beach photos or making sure the lines on a building are perfectly vertical. Just be aware that when you slightly rotate a photo like this, the corners of the image will push outside the rectangular frame. The tool will usually crop the edges slightly to keep the final picture in a perfect rectangle."
