        "h2": "Don't let social media ruin your layout",
        "text": "When you upload a sideways photo to platforms like Instagram or Facebook, it completely throws off your aesthetic. Worse, if you post a backward photo where words are illegible, it looks unprofessional and confusing. Taking thirty seconds to flip or rotate your image before uploading makes a massive difference in how your content is perceived. It shows you care about the details. If you are managing a brand account or a blog, clean, properly oriented imagery is absolutely non-negotiable. Always preview your photos in your camera roll before hitting publish, and run them through a quick online fix if anything looks off."
